## Important transaction boundary

An inquiry is a request for information or coordination.

Accepting an inquiry does not mean:

- A purchase is completed.
- A sale is completed.
- A contract exists.
- Biomass has been reserved.
- Biomass has been collected.
- A collection schedule is confirmed.
- Payment has been made.

Do not automatically deduct or reserve biomass quantities when an inquiry is submitted or accepted.

Preserve the existing database history and auditability of inquiry decisions.

Do not delete historical inquiry records or rewrite their history merely to simplify the interface.

